scope: |
  Three tails, closed together on the owner's instruction:
  1. case-class ctor DEFAULTS are not filled -- `ProcessOptions(None, Map(), None)` emits a struct
     literal missing the defaulted field (E0063). rozum's live meeting server; the machinery that
     fills def-call defaults exists and was simply never applied to constructors.
  2. a LIB crate importing std/json still fails: reachability prunes only where there is an entry
     point, so a library lowers everything its imports brought. Rule: for a lib the roots are the
     defs written in the ROOT module, not what the imports carried in.
  3. `sbt backendRust/test` is not on the push path -- which is HOW my dropped-defaults regression
     survived every push and was found by a sibling instead of by a gate.
next: (1) ctor defaults, (2) import provenance through BackendOptions, (3) the CI step
